    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe acceptance test (`AcceptanceTest.coreComputesDisplayName`) creates an owner via `POST /api/owners` and then `GET /api/owners/{id}`, expecting `$.displayName` to equal `\"LastName, FirstName\"`. I made two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains a `displayName` field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` with an expression on `toOwnerDto(...)` that computes the value as `owner.getLastName() + \", \" + owner.getFirstName()` from the stored names.\n\nBecause both the create response and the `GET` response flow through `toOwnerDto`, the computed `displayName` is returned consistently. Build result: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
